pball/v1.3.2","body":"# QuickMaster 1.3.2\n\nThis release replaces the withdrawn 1.3.1 release.\n\n## Limiter correction\n\n- The route is **Multiband → Broadband → Peak Normalizer** (when enabled).\n- Both limiting stages share the Limit module's input-peak reference. Adding\n  multiband drive no longer raises the broadband ceiling and loses its effect\n  through output normalization. Broadband Push stays independent.\n- Smooth offline lookahead and calibrated release replace the previous\n  depth-dependent timing. The GR display reports actual attenuation, including\n  upstream drive; Push is input gain, not a maximum GR setting.\n- Rendered true peaks are checked, including the end of the file. The final\n  Peak Normalizer remains responsible for the selected delivery ceiling.\n\n## Other improvements since the previous public release\n\n- Upward-only macro RMS Leveler with editable red waveform exclusions,\n  undo/redo and per-track persistence.\n- The waveform follows the processed audio, Bypass and A/B selection.\n- Faster A/B preparation reuses only exact, valid audio; shared edits correctly\n  invalidate cached results.\n- Intervening playback, analysis, export and DSP corrections from the local\n  product audit are included.\n\n## Downloads\n\nDownload and extract the ZIP for your operating system. The application is\nportable and includes Java 25; there is no installer. The core JAR is provided\nfor reproducibility, not as a standalone application. SHA-256 checksums are\nprovided alongside the bundles.\n\nValidation details and limitations are recorded in\n[`docs/diagnostics/limiter-cascade-audit.md`](https://github.com/CristianMoresi/QuickMaster/blob/main/docs/diagnostics/limiter-cascade-audit.md).\n"}
